WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.590
- So you're doing A League of Their Own.

00:00:01.590 --> 00:00:02.700
- [D'Arcy] Yeah.
- This is amazing.

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:03.533
It's on Prime Video.

00:00:03.533 --> 00:00:05.130
So were you so excited to do it?

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:05.963
- So excited.

00:00:05.963 --> 00:00:07.620
One of my favorite movies.

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:09.420
I grew up playing baseball and

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:10.500
- [Kelly] Oh, you did?
- Yeah.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:11.333
- [Kelly] That's awesome.
- Yeah.

00:00:11.333 --> 00:00:13.650
And you know, it's like
baseball and acting

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:15.720
and it just was too good to be true.

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:17.400
- So how is it different from the movie or

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:18.233
is it different?

00:00:18.233 --> 00:00:19.066
- [D'Arcy] It is different,
yeah. It's different.

00:00:19.066 --> 00:00:21.240
I mean, you know, the movie is perfect.

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:23.580
It's one of my faves.

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:26.250
I know people feel very strongly about it,

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:28.320
but it was made 30 years ago.

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:29.880
- What? Oh, I'm old.
- [D'Arcy] Is that right?

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:30.713
Yeah, that's right 30 years ago.

00:00:30.713 --> 00:00:31.560
- That's all I just heard.

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:33.301
- I know, I'm sorry to say that.

00:00:33.301 --> 00:00:34.500
- Oh
- I was like 20, no, 30, 30.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:35.460
- Wow.

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:38.520
- And they had two hours to,
you know, make this movie,

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:39.720
or to tell the story.

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:40.620
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- Not, they didn't have,

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:41.640
they had a little more than two hours

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:42.872
to make the movie actually.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:42.872 --> 00:00:43.705
- Which is just like a small fact

00:00:43.705 --> 00:00:45.100
- [Kelly] They took time.
- that I know.

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:48.977
But we have eight hours
and it's, you know, 2022.

00:00:48.977 --> 00:00:51.210
So, we get into the stories

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:53.640
that weren't told back then.

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:55.500
That were really going on.

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:57.120
Some of the queer stories.

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:00.210
And you know, there's a
scene, this amazing scene,

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:02.910
where a woman picks, this
black woman picks up a ball

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:04.200
and throws it,

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.990
and she has this great arm and we see her

00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:09.180
and then we never see her again.

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:10.013
- [Kelly] Yep.

00:01:10.013 --> 00:01:11.130
- And we get to follow her.

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:12.334
We get to see, you know,

00:01:12.334 --> 00:01:14.000
- [Kelly] I love that.
- her full story.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:15.180
And it's just incredible.

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:16.890
I really am proud to
be a part of this show.

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:18.300
- And you're right
though. It is just a bit,

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:20.370
so you only get so long
and all those characters

00:01:20.370 --> 00:01:22.290
to delve into them is really magical.

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:24.210
- [D'Arcy] Yeah. We really
get to, like, shine a light

00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:26.280
on the stories that we
didn't get to see before.

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:27.113
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:27.113 --> 00:01:27.946
- [D'Arcy] That we haven't gotten to see.

00:01:27.946 --> 00:01:28.779
- [Kelly] And you played baseball,

00:01:28.779 --> 00:01:29.730
you played many sports, like growing up.

00:01:29.730 --> 00:01:30.563
- Yeah. I didn't.

00:01:30.563 --> 00:01:31.920
My, I played baseball and basketball

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:33.750
but my main sport was water polo.

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:34.590
Why am I looking at you?
- Really?

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:36.318
- Yeah. Just in case you're impressed.

00:01:36.318 --> 00:01:37.918
- [Kelly] All that,
all that just let know,

00:01:37.918 --> 00:01:38.751
- [Lester] It's a
Northern California thing.

00:01:38.751 --> 00:01:39.870
- is that you had money.

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:40.703
- Money. No. I think it was

00:01:40.703 --> 00:01:42.630
- Cause no one played
water polo where I'm from.

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:43.860
- [D'Arcy] No, no I think it's

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:44.713
- I don't even know what water polo was.

00:01:44.713 --> 00:01:45.810
- [D'Arcy] Right. All right.

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:47.790
It does sound like, I
think you think it sounds

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:49.320
like a rich person sport because polo

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:51.060
with the horses is that,

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:51.993
- Anything involving horses
usually involves money.

00:01:51.993 --> 00:01:54.900
- This is not horses. There
are no horses in the pool.

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:55.733
- [Kelly] Oh yeah obviously.

00:01:55.733 --> 00:01:56.566
- This is like
- [Kelly] I dunno if I know

00:01:56.566 --> 00:01:57.399
what water polo is. What's water polo?

00:01:57.399 --> 00:01:58.260
- [D'Arcy] I know. A lot of people don't.

00:01:58.260 --> 00:01:59.100
- It's kind of like

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:01.230
soccer in a pool, but with your hands.

00:02:01.230 --> 00:02:02.310
That's what it is.

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:03.210
- That's hard.

00:02:03.210 --> 00:02:04.043
- Yeah. It is hard.

00:02:04.043 --> 00:02:05.250
- Soccer in general is hard enough.

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:06.781
You had to make it worse with water.

00:02:06.781 --> 00:02:07.789
- [D'Arcy] I know, I know.

00:02:07.789 --> 00:02:08.760
We're treading water the whole time.

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:09.821
You can't touch the ground.

00:02:09.821 --> 00:02:10.654
- [Lester] Oh my goodness.

00:02:10.654 --> 00:02:11.850
- I'm gonna say no.
- [D'Arcy] I know.

00:02:11.850 --> 00:02:13.290
- To that magic and fun.

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:14.340
- Yep.

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:15.173
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh.

00:02:15.173 --> 00:02:17.760
So there are LGBTQ stories in the series,

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:18.960
and they're pretty important, right?

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:19.890
- [D'Arcy] Yeah.
- To the storylines.

00:02:19.890 --> 00:02:20.807
- [D'Arcy] For sure, yeah.

00:02:20.807 --> 00:02:21.640
Yeah. A lot, a lot,

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:23.610
a lot of storylines, not just one.

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:24.728
- [Kelly] Oh, that's great.
- Yeah. It's great.

00:02:24.728 --> 00:02:25.561
It's really great.

00:02:25.561 --> 00:02:26.394
- I, I love that.
- [D'Arcy] Yeah.

00:02:26.394 --> 00:02:28.060
- So it's not like the token story.

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:28.893
People feel like, you
know, I hate to say that,

00:02:28.893 --> 00:02:29.767
- [D'Arcy] No, but I mean, it happens

00:02:29.767 --> 00:02:30.750
- But it's cool
- [D'Arcy] all the time.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:31.583
- Yeah.

00:02:31.583 --> 00:02:33.540
- [D'Arcy] A lot of things
that we see in media,

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:35.580
we get to see like just a
little piece of a story,

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:37.260
but we really, we really get into it.

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:38.460
All different kinds of stories.

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:39.600
- [Kelly] I love that.
- I love it too.

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:40.620
I'm really proud of it.

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:43.290
I think people are, it's
connecting with people where,

00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:46.717
you know, social media, you
know, it's good and bad,

00:02:46.717 --> 00:02:49.590
[D'Arcy] but when the show
came out, it just was, it was

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:52.770
we got such a nice
response on social media.

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:55.110
It was really lovely and
touching and the cast

00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:57.660
is sending each other
screenshots and you know, it's

00:02:57.660 --> 00:02:58.920
it's an amazing thing if,

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:01.500
